469.     /// Rolls back pages already linked by [`Self::link_user_pages`] on the error path.
470.     ///
471.     /// Iterates `child`'s user mappings in fixed-size chunks (avoiding any allocation
472.     /// proportional to the mapping set) and unmaps each page that this call could have
473.     /// linked, releasing the shared refcount via the returned `UserFrame`'s `Drop`. A
474.     /// child page is unmapped only when `parent` still has a present user mapping at the
475.     /// same virtual address: every page linked by [`Self::link_user_pages`] is a copy of a
476.     /// parent mapping, so a child page with no counterpart in `parent` is skipped.
477.     ///
478.     /// This `parent`-presence filter is a coarse heuristic, not exact provenance tracking:
479.     /// it cannot tell a page this call installed from a pre-existing `child` mapping that
480.     /// merely happens to overlap a `parent` mapping at the same address — such a page would
481.     /// still be unmapped. That ambiguity is harmless given [`Self::link_user_pages`]'s
482.     /// contract that `child` must not already contain user mappings overlapping `parent`'s,
483.     /// so under correct use the only `child` pages overlapping `parent` are exactly those
484.     /// this call linked. The filter simply avoids tearing down any non-overlapping
485.     /// pre-existing mappings.
