491.     /// PTE state alone is ambiguous, and the shared frame's reference count is not either
492.     /// (e.g. a frame may have had a refcount of 2 from a different child while this child
493.     /// never linked it). Wrongly unmarking a page that another sharer still relies on would
494.     /// break copy-on-write for that sharer, whereas leaving a page copy-on-write that could
495.     /// have been writable merely costs one extra copy-on-write fault on the next write.
496.     /// Since this rollback path is taken only on a rare allocation/mapping failure, that
497.     /// extra fault is negligible, so the safe choice is to never unmark. Steps log and
498.     /// continue on failure to make a best-effort restoration.
499.     fn rollback_linked_pages(parent: &mut Vmem, child: &mut Vmem) {
