542.     /// # Description
543.     ///
544.     /// Attempts to handle a page fault as a copy-on-write fault.
545.     ///
546.     /// A page fault is treated as a copy-on-write fault when it is a user-mode write to
547.     /// a present page whose PTE has the AVL copy-on-write bit set. In that case this
548.     /// function allocates a private frame for the faulting address, copies the contents
549.     /// of the shared frame into it, and points the faulting PTE at the new frame with
550.     /// the writable bit restored and the copy-on-write bit cleared. The reference held
551.     /// on the old shared frame is then released.
552.     ///
553.     /// # Parameters
554.     ///
555.     /// - `vmem`: Virtual memory space of the faulting process.
556.     /// - `fault_addr`: Faulting virtual address (need not be page-aligned).
557.     /// - `error_code`: Typed x86 page-fault error code.
558.     ///
559.     /// # Returns
